WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.496
Delegation is a decision, not a default.

2
00:00:02.776 --> 00:00:14.168
After a year of using an agent for everything, the most valuable skill to build is the one that doesn’t show up in any feature list: deciding what not to hand over, and how much to hand over when you do.

3
00:00:14.448 --> 00:00:21.659
Simon Willison lists “knowing what to outsource” among the practices of engineers who get the most out of coding agents.

4
00:00:21.939 --> 00:00:34.824
This lesson gives you a way to make that call deliberately, looks at what agents do poorly, and then turns to a quieter risk: what heavy delegation does to your own skills, and how to keep growing while you use these tools.
